  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Assertion: The amphoteric behaviour of water&nbsp;is explained by Lewis acid base theory</p><p>Reason: water&nbsp;acts as acid with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and base with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mi>Acid</mi></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#168;</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mi>Base</mi></munder><mo>&#8594;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>OH</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>-</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mrow><mi>Base</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mi>Acid</mi></munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>HS</mi><mo>&#8854;</mo></msup></math></p><p>The amphoteric behaviour of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is explained by Br&oslash;nsted&nbsp;theory not the Lewis acid base theory.</p><p>So, we can say Assertion is false, but reason is true.</p>"
